WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.561 --> 00:00:05.367
(whistling happy tune)

00:00:05.367 --> 00:00:06.730
- The world is pretty evenly divided.

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:08.030
Those that live in rural areas,

00:00:08.030 --> 00:00:09.377
and those that live in cities.

00:00:09.377 --> 00:00:10.979
But how do people decide
which of these two

00:00:10.979 --> 00:00:13.208
will be the right fit for
them, and make them happy?

00:00:13.208 --> 00:00:16.380
Can a place even make you happy?

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:20.958
I dove into research to see who's happier.

00:00:20.958 --> 00:00:23.837
This study says that rural
people are less depressed.

00:00:23.837 --> 00:00:27.181
But then this book shows how
cities make people happier.

00:00:27.181 --> 00:00:29.317
Then again, this study
concludes rural dwellers

00:00:29.317 --> 00:00:30.525
are actually happier.

00:00:30.525 --> 00:00:32.266
So what's the truth?

00:00:32.266 --> 00:00:34.797
We asked people in Los
Angeles about their happiness.

00:00:34.797 --> 00:00:37.165
Well we're here on the
streets of Los Angeles,

00:00:37.165 --> 00:00:40.277
the big city, talking to
people about happiness.

00:00:40.277 --> 00:00:43.643
First question, are you happy?

00:00:43.643 --> 00:00:45.408
(laughter)

00:00:45.408 --> 00:00:47.373
- I mean, I feel like I'm not that happy

00:00:47.373 --> 00:00:48.790
when I'm in the city.

00:00:48.790 --> 00:00:50.810
- Well, I'm actually moving,

00:00:50.810 --> 00:00:53.387
'cause I'm kinda not happy here.

00:00:53.387 --> 00:00:55.422
- Are you happy?
- Very happy.

00:00:55.422 --> 00:00:56.792
- You're very happy.
- I am.

00:00:56.792 --> 00:00:58.371
- Are you happy?

00:00:58.371 --> 00:00:59.690
- Sometimes,

00:00:59.690 --> 00:01:00.688
I wouldn't say all the time.

00:01:00.688 --> 00:01:01.779
Sometimes.

00:01:01.779 --> 00:01:03.288
- So after those mixed answers,

00:01:03.288 --> 00:01:04.519
we headed out to the country,

00:01:04.519 --> 00:01:06.005
stopping at the Halfway House Cafe

00:01:06.005 --> 00:01:09.627
for good old fashioned food
and a chat about happiness.

00:01:09.627 --> 00:01:11.438
So I'm here with Sandy.
- Hello.

00:01:11.438 --> 00:01:12.808
- Are you from around here?

00:01:12.808 --> 00:01:16.082
- Yes. I've lived here for 30 years.

00:01:16.082 --> 00:01:17.847
- Sandy, are you happy?

00:01:17.847 --> 00:01:20.261
- Yes.
- Well there you have it.

00:01:20.261 --> 00:01:21.980
- Are you happy?

00:01:21.980 --> 00:01:23.559
- Absolutely.
- Yeah?

00:01:23.559 --> 00:01:24.479
- Absolutely.

00:01:24.479 --> 00:01:26.104
It's a great area, great place to be.

00:01:26.104 --> 00:01:27.165
- Are you happy?

00:01:27.165 --> 00:01:29.324
- Yeah.
- Oh great.

00:01:29.324 --> 00:01:30.548
- Yeah, I'm happy.

00:01:30.548 --> 00:01:32.382
- The rural people did seem happier,

00:01:32.382 --> 00:01:34.286
but was their happiness actually connected

00:01:34.286 --> 00:01:35.865
to living in the country?

00:01:35.865 --> 00:01:37.281
We asked some of the same people

00:01:37.281 --> 00:01:39.719
if they thought location
affected their happiness.

00:01:39.719 --> 00:01:41.647
- Do you have a lot of hometown pride?

00:01:41.647 --> 00:01:43.551
- Yeah, I do.

00:01:43.551 --> 00:01:45.664
- I went to school here,
my kid went to school here.

00:01:45.664 --> 00:01:47.242
Yeah, I know all these people.

00:01:47.242 --> 00:01:49.861
Yeah, this is my life, this is my town.

00:01:49.861 --> 00:01:54.482
- Do you feel like you'd be
happier in a rural environment?

00:01:54.482 --> 00:01:55.968
- I like the country,

00:01:55.968 --> 00:01:58.754
but the city bring everything.

00:01:58.754 --> 00:02:01.029
You can go to the country,
but not to leave the--

00:02:01.029 --> 00:02:03.421
- I don't really like
going to the city at all.

00:02:03.421 --> 00:02:06.440
- What things make you
happy, do you think?

00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:08.924
- I do a lot of exercise, outdoors.

00:02:08.924 --> 00:02:10.689
So I mean, it just helps me relax,

00:02:10.689 --> 00:02:13.586
and I feel like those
things make me happy.

00:02:13.586 --> 00:02:15.398
- So, it's not really a debate between

00:02:15.398 --> 00:02:16.953
rural and city life.

00:02:16.953 --> 00:02:18.161
People that are happy are often

00:02:18.161 --> 00:02:19.786
just a match to their homes.

00:02:19.786 --> 00:02:20.947
This actually makes sense,

00:02:20.947 --> 00:02:22.735
because the Gallup
Healthways Well-Being Index

00:02:22.735 --> 00:02:24.151
has liking where you live

00:02:24.151 --> 00:02:25.753
as one of the five main indexors

00:02:25.753 --> 00:02:27.680
for overall wellbeing.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:29.863
So if you like where you live,

00:02:29.863 --> 00:02:32.022
you could be one step closer to happiness.

00:02:32.022 --> 00:02:34.066
(whoosh)

00:02:34.066 --> 00:02:38.959
(upbeat piano)

00:02:40.799 --> 00:02:42.744
(scream)

